Z||000004||Cheever3000||08-18-2001||12:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>wow do you put images in posts?????? please esplain step by step.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><B>You again?</B> Why, you neophyte, tenderfoot, wet-behind-the-ears, learners-permit, penny-laggin'...<P>... I forgot what I was gonna say.<P>Oh yeah.  What I do is I click the Pennock's Image Poster square button at the bottom of the screen, see?  Then I <B>print</B> the instructions there.  Okay, with that in hand, I click to get the main download, extract (unzip) it, download the patch, unzip that.  Then I go into Start-Programs-PIP and follow the rest of the instructions.  There are some rare times when a pic won't paste right, and then you go into the PIP History and click that pic, then copy the path shown at the bottom and paste that path like it should have to begin with.  That should do it for you.  The first time is the toughest - just do every little step very slow & easy.  Once you've done it, no big deal after that.<P>Does anybody remember laggin' pennies?<P><BR>||||reg||1
